course: dictionary
lesson: 3417
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word express has more than one meaning, so you need the context to choose the right one. Read the words around it and ask which meaning fits. «Don't grunt, that's not at all a proper way of expressing yourself.» Here express means to show what you think or feel, with words or actions.
explain: The same word can also mean fast. «The parcel went by express delivery and arrived the next day.» Express delivery means the parcel travels quickly, with few stops. An express train is a fast train, so the clues are about speed, not feelings.
explain: In maths, express is a task word. «Express 0.5 as a fraction» tells you to write the same amount in a different form. The value stays the same: 0.5 and one half are equal. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does it still make sense?
fact: Express can be a verb, an adjective or a noun.
fact: «Express yourself» means to show your thoughts or feelings.
fact: «Express delivery» and «an express train» both mean fast.
fact: In maths, «express as» means to change the form of a number but keep its value.
fact: Roots ending in ss take -ssion: express, expression; discuss, discussion.
exercise: «Don't grunt, that's not at all a proper way of expressing yourself.» In this sentence, expressing yourself means? | Writing a number as a fraction | *Showing what you think or feel with words or actions | Travelling on a fast train | Sending a parcel very quickly
exercise: «The parcel went by express delivery and arrived the next day.» Express here means? | *Fast, with few stops | Shown with a happy face | Clearly stated | Written as a decimal
exercise: The maths task says «Express 0.5 as a fraction.» What does express mean in this task? | Say the number out loud | *Change the form, keeping the same value | Round the number to the nearest whole number | Make the number bigger
test: Which word completes the pattern? discuss, discussion; express, ? | expressive | *expression | express train | expressing
test: «The express train reached the city in one hour.» What does express mean here? | A train made of wood | *A fast train | A train that stops at every station | A late train
exam: Ella is asked to express 3/4 as a percentage. What does she need to do? | Make the number smaller | Say the answer out loud | Add 3 and 4 together | *Write the same amount in a different form
